## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical use of CMK with storage in Azure and policy-driven governance across subscriptions; includes rollout, rollback, and testing.

## Key Concepts
- CMK in Azure Key Vault
- Azure Policy with DeployIfNotExists/AuditIfNotExists
- Key rotation, backups, and compliance reporting
- Per-subscription scoping and rollout testing

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyName": "StorageAccounts-CMKBackedEncryption",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/encryption.keySource", "notEquals": "Microsoft.KeyVault"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  },
  "parameters": {
    "keyVault": {"type": "String"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle existing storage accounts that already use platform-managed keys?
- What monitoring/auditing would you add to ensure ongoing CMK compliance?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical guardrails for multi-tenant data platforms, focusing on secure upgrades and leakage controls in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Lighthouse, per-tenant managed identities, least privilege
- Synapse RLS, Data Lake ACLs, per-tenant isolation
- Key Vault rotation, policy gates for secrets in config
- Canary deployments, feature flags, automated rollback
- UEBA monitoring, incident response, runbooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example guardrail check: ensure secrets aren't in config
function validateConfig(config) {
  const forbidden = ['AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY','AZURE_SQL_PASSWORD','SECRET'];
  for (const k of Object.keys(config)) {
    if (forbidden.includes(k.toUpperCase()) || /password|secret|token/i.test(String(config[k]))) {
      throw new Error('Secrets must be stored in Key Vault and not in config');
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test Canary rollback in a live environment with noisy telemetry?
- Which logs and metrics confirm UEBA signals trigger a rollback?

## Why This Is Asked

Probes automated containment and rollback for cross-region, multi-tenant Azure SaaS. Emphasizes real-time orchestration across Key Vault, AAD, RBAC, canaries, and traffic routing.

## Key Concepts

- Defender for Cloud UEBA integrations
- Event Grid and Logic Apps for automation
- Per-tenant Key Vault key rotation and token revocation
- Tenant isolation via RBAC and traffic redirection
- Canary controls and sandbox forensics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo handler for UEBA alert
async function handleUEBAAlert(event) {
  const id = event.tenantId;
  await rotateTenantKeys(id);
  await revokeTenantTokens(id);
  await setTenantRBAC(id, 'read-only');
  await pauseCanariesForTenant(id);
  await redirectTraffic(id, 'lastKnownGood');
  await cloneTenantSandbox(id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this workflow end-to-end?
- How would you audit changes made during containment?
